52†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite54†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L162: \nL163: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2512.15862v1] Reusable theory representations for colliders: a demonstrator SMEFT foundation model (https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15862v1)\nciteturn6504view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15862v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # High Energy Physics - Phenomenology\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 17 Dec 2025]\nL9: # Title:Reusable theory representations for colliders: a demonstrator SMEFT foundation model\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Supratim Das Bakshi , cite6†T.J. Hobbs , cite7†Brandon Kriesten L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Reusable theory representations for colliders: a demonstrator SMEFT foundation model, by Supratim Das Bakshi and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We develop a demonstrator foundation model for collider-scale explorations of the Standard Model Effective Field Theory (SMEFT), constructed from contrastive representations of theoretically simulated neutral-current Drell-Yan cross sections.\nL17: Using a controlled sampling of the Warsaw-basis dimension-6 Wilson-coefficient space at $O(\\Lambda^{-2})$, we generate a corpus of high-resolution differential distributions in $m_{\\ell\\ell}$ and $p_{T}$, augmented by physics-motivated Monte Carlo replicas with correlated uncertainties.\nL18: A minimally parameterized encoder network is trained with a supervised contrastive loss to produce a low-dimensional latent manifold on which SMEFT-induced deformations of the Drell-Yan spectrum acquire a well-defined geometric structure.\nL19: We analyze the resulting embedding and demonstrate that (i) latent directions correlate with characteristic SMEFT shape distortions, including energy-growing four-fermion contributions and electroweak vertex corrections; (ii) clusters in the embedding correspond to families of Wilson-coefficient configurations with similar phenomenological impact; and (iii) the learned representation supports downstream tasks such as classification with uncertainty quantification, anomaly detection, and nearest-neighbor retrieval.\nL20: While restricted to leading-order SMEFT and simplified uncertainty modeling, this study provides the first step toward a reusable, physics-aligned foundational representation for the theory of New-Physics searches at high-energy colliders. We outline extensions towards a complete global analyses, including multi-process training corpora, higher-order corrections, and multi-objective pretraining.\nL21: Comments:  | 39 pages, 12 figures, 2 tables\nL22: Subjects:  | High Energy Physics - Phenomenology (hep-ph)\nL23: Report number:  | ANL-201447\nL24: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2512.15862 [hep-ph]\nL25:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2512.15862v1 [hep-ph] for this version)\nL26:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2512.15862†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL27: ## Submission history\nL28: \nL29: From: Brandon Kriesten [cite13†view email ]\nL30: [v1] Wed, 17 Dec 2025 19:00:03 UTC (5,691 KB)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled Reusable theory representations for colliders: a demonstrator SMEFT foundation model, by Supratim Das Bakshi and 2 other authors\nL37: \nL38:   * cite8†View PDF L39:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L40:   * cite14†TeX Source L41: \nL42: cite15†view license†creativecommons.org L43: ### Current browse 